# Ratchet scripts and their config must check out with LF endings even on
# Windows CI (git-bash). With the default core.autocrlf=true, error-mapping.tsv
# was checked out CRLF, leaving a trailing \r on the last tab-separated field
# (arm_fn); the `awk "/fn $arm_fn/,/^}/"` range then never matched and every
# enum variant was falsely reported as missing a C mapping.
*.sh  text eol=lf
*.tsv text eol=lf
